module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_generated_crossing_call_is_labelled_from_source_text_not_the_callee_parameter

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_generated_crossing_call_is_labelled_from_source_text_not_the_callee_parameter: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_generated_crossing_call_is_labelled_from_source_text_not_the_callee_parameter" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "**A well-typed recursive text function refuses at eval** (INVALID STATE: the v1 seed's generated host-text crossing call `std.coercion.unicode_scalar_unfold(<label>: <arg>)` carries the ARGUMENT's name as its label instead of the callee's declared parameter `s`; HARM: parse, resolve and typecheck all pass and the program dies at eval with `CallContractMismatch { callee: \"unicode_scalar_unfold\", detail: \"no parameter named 'host' (declared: [s])\" }`, so accepted source is refused late and a call reads as a different call). AUTHORABLE RED, one file, no cast and no match: `module v2.probe.f9`, `import std.types { String }`, `import std.logic { Bool }`, `import v2.std.text { string_any_char_in }`, then `fn rec(n: Int, t: String) -> Bool { let host = t  string_any_char_in(s: host, alphabet: \"?\") || (n > 0 && rec(n: n - 1, t: t)) }` and `test fn rec_case() -> Bool { rec(n: 1, t: \"a?\") }`. GREEN control, same file: `fn flat(t: String) -> Bool { let host = t  string_any_char_in(s: host, alphabet: \"?\") }` PASSES. Renaming `host` to `qq_longer_name`, or passing the parameter `t` with no let, changes the reported label to match, so the label tracks the argument's name and not a source offset. Reported by keen-hawk-319 from a real marking witness (`f8.dag`: recursive match over a List, braced arm, let-bound newtype coercion, OR tail that recurses); reproduced 2026-11-05 with `gunbc run --claim-run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <file> --function <test>` on a seed built 2026-11-05 13:11 against origin/main f08a6ae4e44d sources. Not reproduced in earlier probes only because none of them was recursive (keen-hawk-319: the recursive call is the switch).",

    "WHERE IT IS GENERATED AND WHAT IS ESTABLISHED (DESIGN section 6b), hypothesis not yet confirmed to a line: the call is built by `v1.compiler.infer` `host_text_crossing_admitted` (src/v1/04_infer.dag), which labels its argument `param_node_name_at(param, scope.type_env.source_indices)`, i.e. the parameter's identity is READ FROM A SOURCE POSITION (`authored_name_at`: the node's `ident_span` sliced from the `source_indices` entry for `span.file`, falling back to `node.name`). At eval the label is read back by `arg_name_at` through the same slice; the synthetic `<elaborated>` file has no `source_indices` entry, so it falls back to the node name. A name read from a source position is a second authority for the callee parameter's identity (DESIGN section 3): the declaration `unicode_scalar_unfold(s: String)` already owns that fact. Measured so far: the wrong label is already in the generated node, it is not an eval-time rename, and a non-recursive caller of the same shape is correct, so the recursive frame reaches `host_text_crossing_admitted` with a parameter node or index that is not the callee's. NOT yet established: whether that is re-entry with the crossing already applied, a `source_indices` aliasing, or a stale `lookup_func_sig`. The v2 native stages were searched by `git grep` for a generated host-text crossing (`HostText`, `host_text_crossing`, `unicode_scalar_unfold` in src/v2/compiler): `src/v2/compiler/tokenize.dag` and `source_authority.dag` CALL `unicode_scalar_unfold(s: ...)` by hand with the label written, and no v2 stage was found generating the crossing; that is a bounded text search, not a semantic absence proof.",

    "CEILING and NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: decidable and fully modeled (the callee's declared parameters are in `lookup_func_sig`), so a structurally guaranteed rung is attainable: take the label from the declared parameter identity the signature already resolved, never from a span. Next trigger: confirm the discriminating boundary by instrumenting `host_text_crossing_admitted` on the f9 RED, then a one-hunk fix in `v1.compiler.infer` admitted only if the v2 self-host closure exercises this crossing (`gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing`); the RED stays enrolled as the regression control (DESIGN section 4b obligation 4). Until then the rung is unread: the refusal is loud but late and names the wrong cause.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
